<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jérôme Bonaparte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1784">1784</a>–<a href="/years/1860">1860</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jérôme Bonaparte was the youngest brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, who made him king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> from 1807 to 1813, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> as his capital. His kingdom received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1931-constitution-of-ethiopia">first written constitution</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> and introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-code">Napoleonic Code</a>, but was burdened by conscription and war levies. He fled when Russian troops took Kassel in 1813, and late in life he became a marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> under his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jerome-bonaparte.jpg" alt="Jérôme Bonaparte" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Gérard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Jerome_Bonaparte.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
